== Notes ==
* All {{R|Crawl Space}} trapdoors on a floor lead to the same {{R|Crawl Space}}.
* It can be used in {{s|Depths}} II to access {{s|Womb}} even before defeating {{e|Mom}} and gaining the achievement which 'unlocks' the Womb.
* If used in {{s|Womb}} II / {{s|Utero}} II / {{s|Scarred Womb}} II, the trapdoor will always lead to {{s|Sheol}}.
* {{dlc|nr}} Has no effect in the {{s|Cathedral}}, {{s|Chest}}, {{s|Sheol}}, {{s|Dark Room}}, {{s|???}} and {{s|The Void}} (no trapdoors of any type will be generated).
* {{dlc+|r}} It can only create crawl space trapdoors in the {{s|Cathedral}}, {{s|Chest}}, {{s|Sheol}}, {{s|Dark Room}}, {{s|???}}, {{s|The Void}}, {{s|Corpse}} II, {{i|Dad's Note}} floor, {{s|Home}}, and during the [[Ascent]]. However the chance for the crawl space trapdoor to appear does not change.{{dlc-}}
* Using the item on the 3 tiles directly horizontal to a door, including {{R|Secret Room}} entrances, will cause the trapdoor to spawn in a random spot next to Isaac instead, making this item an indirect aid to locating Secret Rooms.
** {{dlc|r}} If a special graphic is in these spots, the trapdoor will likely be moved to a spot that won't spawn a {{R|Crawl Space}}.
** Spawning enough trapdoors can cause a trapdoor to spawn in these spots.
* This item can be used to destroy [[rocks]] if used while Isaac is [[flight|flying]] over a rock.
* If a crawlspace is spawned before activating a {{r|Challenge Room}} or {{r|Boss Challenge Room}}, the crawlspace will remain open during the fight. Entering and exiting the crawlspace skips the fights entirely.
* {{dlc|nr}} When used on the last floor of a [[Challenges|challenge]], a trapdoor to the next floor can spawn. If it is entered, Isaac must beat the boss of that floor to spawn the ending trophy.
* {{Dlc|r}} Trapdoors will not spawn on challenges on floors at the final destination, however certain challenges like [[Red Redemption]] may still spawn a trapdoor leading to the next floor.

== Synergies ==
* {{Book of Virtues synergy|description=Spawns a skull wisp on the middle ring that shoots bone tears.}}
* {{I|Lil Portal|r+}}: upon entering a trap door (not a Crawl Space), inside the Lil Portal special room, Isaac will be teleported to the {{r|I AM ERROR}} Room.

== Interactions ==
* {{I|Car Battery}}: In most cases, no extra effect. When used near the entrances to a room, the item can occasionally open 2 trapdoors at once, {{Dlc|nr}} increasing the chance of opening a {{r|Crawl Space}}.

